WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.230
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:23.110
to air in 2022. Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan
Condal will serve as showrunners and executive

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.740
producers.
George R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.720
producer.
It’s based on George RR Martin’s Targaryen

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.820
history book Fire And Blood volume 1
and on Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.079
Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:41.940
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.690
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.350
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:56.679
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:00:56.679 --> 00:01:02.410
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:07.740
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:14.140
The key event of the prequel will be the Dance
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.600
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.990
The war of succession between Aegon II and
his half-sister Rhaenyra over their father

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:27.550
Viserys I's throne.
Targaryens fought Targaryens, brothers fought

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:32.520
brothers, dragons fought dragons.
Most of Westeros waged war in either support

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.130
of Queen Rhaenyra and became known as the
''blacks''

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.619
or in support of her rival King Aegon II and
became known as the ''greens'',

00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:42.890
and by the time it was over dozens of thousands
were dead,

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.360
most of the dragons were killed as well as
most of Targaryens.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.400
The biggest supporter of King Aegon II and
the man who fought the most for the ''greens''

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.740
as well as burned the most of Westeros in
this war, was King Aegon's brother Aemond.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:00.649
Prince Aemond Targaryen, also known as Aemond
One-Eye or Aemond the Kinslayer,

00:02:00.649 --> 00:02:05.680
was a Prince of the Targaryen dynasty who
rode the most powerful dragon of its time,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.700
mighty Vhagar.
Vhagar was a she-dragon of House Targaryen.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.590
She was ridden by Queen Visenya Targaryen
during Aegon's Conquest,

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:18.800
alongside Aegon the Conqueror's Balerion and
their sister Rhaenys's Meraxes.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.660
Prince Aemond and his dragon Vhagar played
a major role in the Targaryen civil war.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.510
By the time of the Dance of the Dragons, Vhagar
was the hardened survivor of a hundred battles,

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:34.270
had grown almost as large as Balerion, and
was the oldest and largest of dragons in Westeros.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:39.550
Her roar was so powerful that it could shake
the very foundations of Storm's End.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.280
No living dragon could match her for size
or ferocity.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:49.050
Born in 110 AC, Aemond was the second son
of King Viserys I Targaryen and Queen Alicent

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.390
Hightower and the brother of King Aegon II
Targaryen.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:57.760
At birth, Aemond was said to be half the size
his older brother, Aegon, had been,

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.422
although he was twice as fierce.
The births of Aemond and his older brother

00:03:01.422 --> 00:03:07.290
Aegon were the cause of some strife at the
court of Viserys I. The king had named Rhaenyra,

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:13.340
his only surviving child by his first marriage,
his official heir in 105 AC, but refused to

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.380
change the order of succession after the birth
of two healthy sons.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.040
This eventually led to the rise of the "queen's
party" at the royal court,

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:26.320
as opposed to the "princess's party".
In 120 AC, when Aemond was ten years old,

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.610
his brother-in-law, Ser Laenor Velaryon, died.
Aemond accompanied his parents and siblings

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:37.370
to Driftmark to attend Laenor's funeral.
King Viserys had suggested traveling to Dragonstone

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:41.730
after the funeral, and informed Aemond,
who out of all his siblings was the only one

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.250
yet without a dragon of his own,
that he could claim a dragon egg or hatchling

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:51.630
on Dragonstone for his own, if he was "bold
enough". Annoyed by his father's comment,

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:57.260
Aemond resolved to claim Vhagar, the oldest
and largest living dragon, who had recently

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:03.110
become riderless with the death of Laena Velaryon.
Vhagar was present on Driftmark,

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:06.980
and Aemond who knew that his parents would
not allow him near the dragon,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:11.830
went to make his attempt in secret. Aemond
was caught by his three-year-old nephew, Prince

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:15.040
Joffrey.
In an attempt to keep him quiet, Aemond slapped

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.150
and threatened the younger boy before shoving
him into a pile of dragon droppings. When

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:25.770
Joffrey began to yell, Aemond climbed on top
of Vhagar's back. The dragon broke free of

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:29.040
her chains, and Aemond flew two circles before
landing.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:35.379
Joffrey, however, had alarmed his two older
siblings, Jacaerys and Lucerys Velaryon.

00:04:35.379 --> 00:04:41.020
The four boys fought with wooden training
swords, until Aemond called his nephews "Strongs"

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:45.330
as it was rumored they were bastards of their
mother's lover Ser Harwin Strong,

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:50.289
having their rumored father's appearance rather
than Valyrian appearance of House Targaryen

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:55.599
or Velaryion. Jacaerys, old enough to understand
the insult, attacked Aemond again.

00:04:55.599 --> 00:04:59.620
When Aemond gained the upper hand and began
to beat Jacaerys savagely,

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:05.520
Lucerys drew his dagger and slashed at Aemond's
face, taking out his right eye.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.879
After the incident, Queen Alicent called for
Lucerys to lose an eye as penance,

00:05:09.879 --> 00:05:14.880
which King Viserys refused, while Princess
Rhaenyra demanded that Aemond was questioned,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.449
"sharply", until he revealed where he heard
her sons being described as "Strongs" –

00:05:19.449 --> 00:05:22.509
as naming them such was suggesting they were
bastards,

00:05:22.509 --> 00:05:27.199
and therefore that Rhaenyra was guilty of
high treason by sleeping with Ser Harwin Strong.

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:31.599
Forced by his father, Aemond eventually admitted
hearing the name from his brother, Prince

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:34.789
Aegon.
While he was an unforgiving person, Aemond

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:37.229
would later say that he considered losing
an eye

00:05:37.229 --> 00:05:42.030
to be a fair trade in an exchange for obtaining
the great Vhagar.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:47.520
Afterward he often put a smoothed sapphire
as a false eye in his empty socket.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.639
Despite the loss of his eye, Aemond went on
to become one of the most fearsome swordsmen

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:57.090
in all of Westeros, as he spent the next ten
years being trained by Ser Criston Cole, Lord

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:01.990
Commander of the Kingsguard.
On the first day of 127 AC, King Viserys held

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:08.409
a feast to celebrate the return of his health.
After the King had left the feast, Aemond

00:06:08.409 --> 00:06:12.469
toasted his three Velaryon cousins,
speaking of their appearance, mocking them

00:06:12.469 --> 00:06:17.120
as "three Strong boys".
Aemond wore night-black armor, chased with

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.240
gold.
In 129 AC, when Aemond was nineteen years

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.210
old, his father, King Viserys I Targaryen
died.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:29.680
Aemond's older brother was crowned King Aegon
II Targaryen despite their older sister Rhaenyra

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.479
having been Viserys's chosen heir, starting
the war of succession known as the Dance of

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:37.889
the Dragons.
At the beginning of the war Aemond flew Vhagar

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:41.370
to Storm's End
to win the loyalty of Lord Borros Baratheon

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:46.020
by wedding one of his daughters.
Rhaenyra's second son Lucerys also arrived

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:50.400
on his dragon Arrax,
with the same goal of winning over the Baratheons.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.669
Lucerys, however, only asked Borros to join
Rhaenyra for the sake of his past oaths,

00:06:55.669 --> 00:07:00.199
and said he could not wed one of his daughters
because he was already betrothed so Borros

00:07:00.199 --> 00:07:04.309
spurned his offer.
When Aemond threatened Lucerys, stating he

00:07:04.309 --> 00:07:07.430
owed him an eye,
Borros refused to allow them to fight under

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:11.539
his roof.
Borros's men restrained Aemond, allowing Lucerys

00:07:11.539 --> 00:07:15.849
to leave the hall
and take off on his dragon, Arrax. When Borros's

00:07:15.849 --> 00:07:20.610
daughter Maris taunted Aemond,
asking him if Lucerys had removed his balls

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:26.319
as well as his eye, Aemond became enraged.
When he asked Borros's leave, Borros told

00:07:26.319 --> 00:07:29.539
Aemond that he had no say about what Aemond
did

00:07:29.539 --> 00:07:33.529
while not underneath Borros's roof, and allowed
him to depart.

00:07:33.529 --> 00:07:39.310
Aemond mounted Vhagar and pursued his cousin,
avenging the loss of his eye by killing Lucerys

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:44.960
and Arrax. Mushroom claims Aemond located
the boy's corpse and removed both of his eyes

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.309
to present them to Lady Maris on a bed of
seaweed.

00:07:48.309 --> 00:07:52.029
Aemond was known thereafter as a kingslayer
among his enemies.

00:07:52.029 --> 00:07:57.460
His own mother, Alicent Hightower and grandfather
Otto Hightower were horrified by Aemond's

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:01.870
actions; they'd still hoped the war might
be ended diplomatically, but by killing one

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:06.210
of her sons, Aemond had ensured Rhaenyra would
fight to the bitter end.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:11.020
Otto Hightower famously told him ''You only
lost one eye, how could you be so blind?''

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.539
Aemond and Vhagar's next major fight was in
the Battle of Rook's Rest,

00:08:14.539 --> 00:08:20.180
where Aegon II's armies set a trap for Rhaenys
Targaryen riding the dragon Maelys.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:26.759
When she arrived she was ambushed two-on-one
by Aegon II riding Sunfyre and Aemond on Vhagar.

00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:32.300
Even so, Maelys was a large dragon and did
not go down without a fight:

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.790
at the end of their fall to the ground, Vhagar
was relatively unharmed,

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:41.180
but Sunfyre was crippled and nearly killed.
Aegon II himself was burned over half of his

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:44.380
body,
leaving him semi-conscious for the next full

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:49.910
year as he slowly recovered.
In his stead, at Alicent's behest Aemond stepped

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:53.370
up to become Prince Regent
and Protector of the Realm.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:58.250
As Prince Regent, Aemond gathered an army
together with Ser Criston Cole, the Hand of

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:01.510
the King.
Now in command, Aemond demonstrated that as

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:06.970
a swordsman and a dragonrider he was a deadly
opponent, but also a hothead with no sense

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:10.390
of strategy.
He decided that the real threat was not Rhaenyra

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:14.270
on Dragonstone to the east,
but the main armies of her supporters massing

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:20.040
under his uncle Daemon at Harrenhal.
Therefore, he led out all of Aegon II's remaining

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:25.240
armies in the Crownlands north to attack Harrenhall
- leaving the capital city with only a skeleton

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:29.040
defense.
Daemon however had planned on this and simply

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:33.100
abandoned Harrenhal,
his army moving to the west where it destroyed

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.850
the Lannisters' armies.
Meanwhile, Daemon himself flew his dragon

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.870
to King's Landing,
where Rhaenyra's small fleet in the east,

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:43.930
augmented by dragons,
was able to capture the lightly defended city.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.330
There was no siege, as the City Watch were
loyal to Daemon

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:51.770
and supported Daemon as soon as he appeared.
He made his niece and wife, Rhaenyra, the

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:55.650
Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.
Aemond arrived at Harrenhal to find an empty

00:09:55.650 --> 00:10:00.140
castle, and quickly heard the news of the
loss of King's Landing as well as destruction

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:04.320
of their forces in the west.
Aemond was driven into such a rage at his

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:08.950
failure that he nearly killed the messenger
who brought the news. In petty revenge he

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:12.400
then used Vhagar to burn every wooden structure
in Harrenhal –

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.230
the second time the castle was blasted by
dragonflame.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:20.290
Aemond then impetuously abandoned his main
army to launch a one-man / one-dragon war

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:26.010
against Rhaenyra's followers in the Riverlands,
burning out entire towns and personally destroying

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:30.710
vast swaths of territory.
With him he took his bedmate, the seer Alys

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:34.690
Rivers. While devastating, even this proved
to be folly:

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:39.920
the army he had taken north to Harrenhal was
left to retreat south through the Riverlands,

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:44.350
with no dragon to defend it. Rhaenyra's forces
in the region managed to loop around from

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:49.970
defeating the Lannisters and surround Cole's
army: outnumbered three to one Aegon II's

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:55.250
remaining army was wiped out in a decisive
battle, and Cole himself killed.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:59.930
Daemon hunted long for Aemond and Vhagar,
but Aemond would flee ahead of him and other

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:04.930
searchers - he knew that Vhagar could kill
any dragon in a one on one fight, and his

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:09.340
hit-and-run attacks would draw out two or
three of Rhaenyra's other dragons from other

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:14.540
fronts in the war as they hunted him in vain.
Eventually, despairing of the war, Daemon

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:20.279
waited alone with his dragon Caraxes in the
ruins of Harrenhal as a challenge to Aemond

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:23.830
– knowing that Aemond would only face him
in a one-on-one fight

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:28.050
he thought he could win because his dragon
was the oldest and biggest of the remaining

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:31.301
dragons,
being almost the size of Balerion, but he

00:11:31.301 --> 00:11:36.460
was wrong as Daemon's dragon was just as fierce
and battle proven. Aemond could never dare

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:41.400
to duel Daemon 1 on 1 with a sword on foot
as Daemon was the best warrior in this time

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:46.640
period and Aemond knew it,
but Aemond had another advantage - Vhagar

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:52.400
- but not even that was enough to beat Daemon.
After thirteen days Aemond arrived, along

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:56.680
with a pregnant Alys.
She stayed on the ground as Aemond and Daemon

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:01.280
took to the air for the final, mighty duel
between Vhagar and Caraxes.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:05.880
In Aemond's final exchange with his uncle
Daemon, he said to him "You have lived too

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:09.500
long, uncle."
and Daemon replied "On that much, we agree."

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:14.070
It was an aerial duel that took place in the
skies above Harrenhal and the Gods Eye

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:17.760
between two of the most powerful living dragons,
Vhagar and Caraxes,

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:21.970
and their riders, Prince Aemond and Prince
Daemon Targaryen.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:26.330
The duel was said to be a sight to see. The
sun was setting as the two dragons took to

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.590
the sky.
So bright was the dragonfire that smallfolk

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:34.460
feared the sky was aflame.
When Caraxes attacked Vhagar, she ripped upon

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:39.480
his stomach and tore one of his wings,
but then Caraxes fastened his jaws around

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:44.190
her throat in a death grip.
These injuries forced them both to cease flying

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:48.370
and as they tumbled to the water below,
Daemon dueled Aemond to death.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:54.380
At the climax of the fight, as he never fastened
his saddle, Daemon stood up on Caraxes

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:58.910
and leaped at Aemond, whereupon he drove his
Dark Sister through Aemond's eye

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:02.530
and through his neck, just a second before
hitting the water.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:07.490
Aemond's body that was still chained to the
saddle, went underwater along with Vhagar,

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:13.110
was only recovered years after the war, with
Dark Sister still impaled through his skull.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:18.040
The Battle Above the Gods Eye ended in the
deaths of both riders and both dragons.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:23.620
Aemond was 20 years old when he died.
Daemon was forty-nine when he died.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:27.020
Unlike Aemond's body, however, Daemon's was
never found.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:31.470
Singers say that Daemon lived to spend the
rest of his days in secret with Nettles,

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:36.100
but most historians disagree.
What happened to Aemond's child with Alys

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:39.510
as well as with Alys herself remains yet to
be seen.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:43.310
Aemond is definitely going to be one of the
most important characters in the upcoming

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:46.050
prequel show.
Let me know your thoughts about all of this

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.930
in the comment section down below.
Thank you so much for watching, if you enjoyed

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:58.250
this video please give it a big thumbs up
and I hope to see you in the next one. Peace!

